
# 2025-11-22 03:52:50.061552
+Code the following app
+```
+Build a Chainlink price feed dashboard for BTC, ETH, and SOL.
+Architecture:
+Server-side API route: app/api/prices/[symbol]/route.ts handles RPC calls
+Client component: components/price-dashboard.tsx displays prices and graphs
+Shared config: lib/feeds.ts exports contract addresses
+RPC endpoint:
+Use https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com (free, no auth)
+Method selector: 0x50d25bcd for Chainlink's latestRoundData()
+Handle both full (322 chars) and truncated (66 chars) hex responses
+Contract addresses:
+BTC: 0xF4030086522a5bEEa4988F8cA5B36dbC97BeE88c
+ETH: 0x5f4eC3Df9cbd43714FE2740f5E3616155C5b8419
+SOL: 0x4ffC43a60e009B551865A93d232E33Fce9f01507
+Features:
+API route: fetch price from RPC, parse hex response, return JSON {price: number, symbol: string}
+Dashboard: display prices with $ prefix, update every 30 seconds
+Graph: plot price history on canvas with 10% padding (top/bottom and price range)
+Moving dot: green dot with glow at latest price point (rightmost)
+Hover/tap: yellow crosshair and price tooltip on hover (desktop) or tap (mobile)
+localStorage: persist history, handle parsing errors gracefully
+Requirements:
+TypeScript strict mode compliant (no any types)
+Proper error handling (no crashes on API failures)
+Mobile-friendly touch events
+Clean code with no unused variables
+Build this step by step, starting with the API route, then the dashboard component.
+```
+
+Generate an app logo and update the app metadata title and description.

